-- =============================================================================
-- Shared migration 045 — sql_type backfill, plus the invoice_type/supply_type
-- vocabulary gap and the currency format check migrations 031/044 make real.
--
-- THIS IS A DATA CORRECTION, generated by re-running
-- `src/catalogue/field_constraints.py`'s derivation against live DDL and
-- diffing every DERIVED field's row against what migration 042 seeded —
-- 326 of them move. Migration 042 is untouched: it is applied and
-- checksum-pinned, and this is the delta CLAUDE.md calls for instead of
-- regenerating it. `document_type_rule` gets no INSERT here — the derivation
-- run found zero new multi-column rules, only field-level corrections.
--
-- THREE THINGS MOVE, ALL FROM CODE FIXED THE SAME COMMIT:
--
--   1. `sql_type` (migration 044) populates for every DERIVED field that has
--      a column — it was a brand new NULL column, so this is the ENTIRE
--      backfill, not a narrow fix. This is what makes `SALES_REGISTER`'s
--      `line_number`/`qty` legible as `integer`/`numeric` rather than only
--      inferable from `numeric_precision`/`numeric_scale` — the ERP upload
--      E2E suite's finding (2026-09-01) that `data_type = 'text'` alone
--      does not say a field is actually numeric.
--
--   2. `invoice_type`/`supply_type` (SALES_REGISTER) now carry
--      `allowed_values`. `field_constraints.py` previously read only CHECK
--      constraints (`contype = 'c'`); these two columns are constrained by a
--      FOREIGN KEY to `platform_ref.universal_master` instead (tenant
--      migration 009's `<col>_vt` pinning pattern), which a CHECK-only
--      reading of `pg_constraint` never saw. The vocabulary was always
--      enforced by the database — this migration is the derivation catching
--      up to that, not a new rule.
--
--   3. `currency` (SALES_REGISTER) gains `pattern = '^[A-Z]{3}$'`, following
--      tenant migration 031's new CHECK on the column. See that migration's
--      header for why this is a format rule, not an invented vocabulary —
--      no specimen in this repo says what currencies a sales register may
--      carry, so no list is published, only the shape ISO 4217 codes share.
-- =============================================================================

-- 326 rows updated.

